// Type inconnu pour la question EM U4 p33 Review 4.0 Key word transformation (description)
::EM U4 p33 Review 4.0 Key word transformation:: Complete the second sentence so that it has a similar meaning to the first sentence, using the word given. Do not change the word given. You must use between two and five words, including the word given. Here is an example: <blockquote>Please don’t drive so fast — this is a dangerous road.<br> <b>MORE</b><br> Please <i>drive more slowly</i> — this is a dangerous road.</blockquote> {}

// Type inconnu pour la question EM U5 p34 Voc1.0 (description)
::EM U5 p34 Voc1.0:: Complete sentences with the words in the list. {}

::EM U5 p34 Voc1.1:: I never eat meat — I follow a strict ___ diet. { ~high-fat ~low-salt ~ =vegetarian ~vitamins ~well-balanced }

::EM U5 p34 Voc1.3:: It’s good to give children a ___ diet, including meat, frurt and sugar. { ~high-fat ~low-salt ~vegetarian ~vitamins ~ =well-balanced }

::EM U5 p34 Voc1.4:: love frurt, vegetables and so on, I know I’m getting a diet rich in ___ . { ~high-fat ~low-salt ~vegetarian ~ =vitamins ~well-balanced }

::EM U5 p34 Voc1.5:: Older people may be advised to follow a ___ diet for health reasons. { ~high-fat ~ =low-salt ~vegetarian ~vitamins ~well-balanced }

// Type inconnu pour la question EM U5 p38 Gra2 passive forms (description)
::EM U5 p38 Gra2 passive forms:: Complete the email with the correct active or passive form of the verbs in brackets. {}

// Type inconnu pour la question EM U5 p38 Gra3.0 passive (description)
::EM U5 p38 Gra3.0 passive:: Complete the second sentence so that it has a similar meaning to the first sentence, using the word given. Do not change the word given. You must use between two and five words, including the word given. {}

::EM U5 p38 Gra3.1 passive:: The chef gave him the recipe. (WAS) He ___ the chef. { =was given the recipe by }

::EM U5 p38 Gra3.2 passive:: The lecture about healthy food raised many interesting issues. (BROUGHT) Many interesting issues ___ the lecture about healthy food. { =were brought up in =were brought up by =were brought up during }

::EM U5 p38 Gra3.3 passive:: Mary baked the cake using six eggs. (BAKED) The cake ___ who used six eggs. { =was baked by Mary }

::EM U5 p38 Gra3.4 passive:: You can't smoke anywhere in the restaurant. (PERMITTED) Smoking ___ anywhere in the restaurant. { =is not permitted }

::EM U5 p38 Gra3.5 passive:: Please check that someone has washed up before you leave! (DONE) Please check that the ___ before Rafa joined him as his business partner. { =washing-up has been done =washing up has been done }

::EM U5 p38 Gra3.6 passive:: Jo had opened the restaurant by himself before Rafa joined him as hs business partner. (HAD) The restaurant ___ Jo before Rafa joined him as his business partner. { =had been opened by }

// Type inconnu pour la question EM U6 p46-47 4.0 UoE Key word transformation (description)
::EM U6 p46-47 4.0 UoE Key word transformation:: Complete the second sentence so that it has a similar meaning to the first sentence, using the word given. Do not change the word given.You must use between two and five words, including the word given.<br> <blockquote> A very kind friend took us home after the party. (<b>TAKEN</b>)<br> Aften the party, we <i><u>were taken home by</u></i> a very kind friend. </blockquote> {}

